  "source_assessment": [
    "The two aliases express no invariant beyond ConnectionPeer and the removed spawn_peer functions return its spawn directly. Direct calls retain the same eager acquisition and Future/Drop/stop behavior.",
    "EnvironmentRelay and TunnelPeer encode actual relay/result responsibilities; spawn_relay performs an actual io::Result-to-TestResult conversion and remains.",
    "All21 named tests retain ordered operations, literal request/response/frame/data/head assertions, finite bounds and classified causes after the explicit substitutions.",
    "Returned errors still combine primary and concrete cleanup causes through the existing owner; inherited deliberate disconnect classifications remain narrow and unchanged.",
    "Manual paragraphs separate snapshot acquisition from source mutation, selected route from real exchange, status/body from completion, H2 response preparation from completion witness, and observation from fallback/cleanup/assertions.",
    "The relocated OK constant preserves the exact literal before responsibilities; no behavioral flag, dependency, shared API or generic task layer is introduced."
  ],
